### Binaries ###
# Only the real output directory. A binary in the REPO ROOT is deliberately NOT
# ignored: it can only get there from a wrong build — `go build ./cmd/<pkg>`
# with no -o (which names the output after the package directory), or a
# hand-typed -o. Every supported path writes into dist/bin, so an artifact at
# the root is a mistake, and ignoring it just hides the mistake — a 40 MB
# citeck-desktop sat untracked in the root for days that way. Let it show up in
# git status instead.
/dist/

